Added 59 lines of output to the chat.
The error occurs because the ComplexConv2d module's internal nn.Conv2d expects  
the input to have 2 * in_channels channels, but the BasicBlock is passing the   
output of the previous ComplexConv2d (which has 2 * out_channels channels)      
directly to the next ComplexConv2d without adjusting the in_channels parameter  
correctly in the ResNet's _make_layer logic.                                    

Specifically, in ResNet._make_layer, when complex_conv=True, self.in_planes is  
updated to planes * 2. However, the BasicBlock constructor takes in_planes and  
planes. If in_planes is 128 (which is 64 * 2), and planes is 64, the BasicBlock 
creates a ComplexConv2d(128, 64, ...). Inside ComplexConv2d, it creates         
nn.Conv2d(2 * 128, 4 * 64, ...) which expects input with 256 channels. But the  
actual input tensor coming from the previous layer has 128 channels (since the  
previous ComplexConv2d output was 2 * 64 = 128).                                

The issue is that ComplexConv2d is designed to take in_channels as the number of
complex channels, so the real input tensor should have 2 * in_channels channels.

In BasicBlock, self.conv1 is ComplexConv2d(in_planes, planes, ...).             

If in_planes is the number of complex channels, the input tensor must have 2 *  
in_planes channels.                                                             

In ResNet, self.in_planes is initialized to 64.                                 

conv1 is ComplexConv2d(1, 64, ...). Input has 2 channels. Output has 2 * 64 =   
128 channels.                                                                   

Then self.in_planes should be updated to 64 (the number of complex channels),   
not 128.                                                                        

Wait, in _make_layer:                                                           

layers.append(block(in_planes, planes, stride, self.complex_conv))              

If in_planes is 64 (complex), block creates ComplexConv2d(64, 64, ...).         

ComplexConv2d(64, 64) expects input with 2 * 64 = 128 channels.                 

The input from conv1 has 128 channels. This matches.                            

Then self.in_planes is updated to planes * 2 in the current code. This is wrong.
It should be updated to planes (the number of complex channels).                

Let's trace:                                                                    

 1 ResNet.__init__: self.in_planes = 64.                                        
 2 conv1 = ComplexConv2d(1, 64, ...). Input: 2 ch. Output: 128 ch.              
 3 layer1 = self._make_layer(BasicBlock, 64, 3, stride=1).                      
    • Inside _make_layer: in_planes = self.in_planes (64).                      
    • block(64, 64, 1, True).                                                   
    • Inside BasicBlock: conv1 = ComplexConv2d(64, 64, ...). Expects input 128  
      ch.                                                                       
    • Input is 128 ch. OK.                                                      
    • conv2 = ComplexConv2d(64, 64, ...). Expects input 128 ch.                 
    • Output of conv1 is 128 ch. OK.                                            
    • self.in_planes update in _make_layer: self.in_planes = planes * 2 -> 128. 
    • Next block in layer1: block(128, 64, 1, True).                            
    • Inside BasicBlock: conv1 = ComplexConv2d(128, 64, ...). Expects input 2 * 
      128 = 256 ch.                                                             
    • But input is 128 ch. Error.                                               

So the fix is: self.in_planes should track the number of complex channels.      

After ComplexConv2d(in, out), the output has 2 * out real channels, which       
corresponds to out complex channels.                                            

So self.in_planes should be set to planes, not planes * 2.                      

Also, the shortcut connection in BasicBlock needs to match the number of complex
channels.                                                                       

If in_planes != planes, we need a ComplexConv2d(in_planes, planes, 1, stride).  

This will output 2 * planes real channels.                                      

The main path outputs 2 * planes real channels.                                 

So the addition out += self.shortcut(x) works.                                  

Let's update ResNet._make_layer and ResNet.__init__ to use complex channel      
counts.                                                                         

